WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Why can a quiet person still take the stage?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
One label cannot cover every situation.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Trait research describes relatively stable tendencies.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
It also examines people in situations.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Tendencies can help explain differences.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
One person may seek company and solitude.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Goals, familiarity and support can change behavior.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Continuous scales often fit traits better than two boxes.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
This scale is illustrative, not your test score.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Quiet does not automatically mean socially unable.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
Outgoing does not mean always wanting a crowd.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
A short quiz cannot determine a life path.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Describe yourself with the situation included.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Look at tendencies across time as well.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Measurement needs evidence suited to its purpose.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
You can have tendencies and try something new.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Self-understanding can make choices more specific.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Loosen the label. Leave room for change.
